WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.212
In 1521, an expedition sent west to reach the Spice Islands was falling apart.

2
00:00:06.812 --> 00:00:20.111
Its commander, Ferdinand Magellan, had been killed on Mactan. After a run of command changes, a ship's master named Juan Sebastián Elcano was captain of the Victoria.

3
00:00:20.711 --> 00:00:36.631
At Tidore the other ship was leaking. The Victoria would go home alone: west, by the Portuguese route, without calling at any port. Sixty men went aboard.

4
00:00:37.231 --> 00:00:50.449
For about nine weeks, gales held her off the Cape of Good Hope. Scurvy spread and the ship leaked. The crew begged him to put in at Mozambique. He refused.

5
00:00:51.049 --> 00:01:02.742
Starving, they stopped at Portuguese Cape Verde, and found their calendar a day behind. When the Portuguese seized the boat's crew, Elcano cut the cable and left them.

6
00:01:03.342 --> 00:01:11.061
On 6 September 1522 the Victoria reached Sanlúcar. Eighteen men came home.

7
00:01:11.661 --> 00:01:20.161
Magellan planned the voyage and died on it. Elcano finished it. They had sailed right round the world.
